  "result": "Perfect! All 119 tests pass. I've successfully implemented VAT calculations across the invoicing system:\n\n**Added to `src/invoices.js`:**\n- New `lineVAT(line)` function that calculates VAT on line amount AFTER discount\n  - Formula: roundCents((lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100)\n  - Result clamped at 0\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n  - `vat` = sum of all line VATs (each rounded independently)\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n**Updated `src/render.js`:**\n- Shows per-line VAT when vatRate > 0%\n- Shows invoice-level VAT summary line when total VAT > 0\n- Displays VAT line just above the total, after discount line\n\n**Key implementation details:**\n- VAT computed per-line on amount AFTER discount\n- Each line's VAT independently rounded with `roundCents()`\n- Invoice VAT is sum of rounded line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n- All amounts never go below 0 (clamped at 0)\n- Formula: total = subtotal - discount + vat\n\n**Tests added (15 new VAT tests):**\n- lineVAT calculations with various discount/VAT scenarios\n- invoiceTotals with VAT included\n- invoiceTotals with multiple lines and different VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n- VAT-exempt items\n- Rendering VAT in text output\n- Integration of discount + VAT calculations\n\nAll 119 tests pass. Ready for the next request!",
